{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לתת לו פי שנים", :translit "latet lo pi shnayim", :gloss "to give him a double portion"} {:he "בכור", :translit "bekhor", :gloss "firstborn"} {:he "בי\"ת", :translit "bet", :gloss "letter bet"} {:he "כ\"ף", :translit "kaf", :gloss "letter kaf"} {:he "יו\"ד", :translit "yod", :gloss "letter yod"} {:he "רי\"ש", :translit "resh", :gloss "letter resh"} {:he "וי\"ו", :translit "vav", :gloss "letter vav"} {:he "שני ווי\"ן", :translit "shnei vavin", :gloss "two vavs"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Orthographic observation: each letter of בכור exhibits doubling — bet doubled over preceding letter, kaf over preceding yod, resh likewise, and vav written as two vavs"}], :frame {:text "The law of the firstborn's double portion is stated in Deuteronomy 21:17. The observation about the orthographic form of בכור is Ba'al HaTurim's own structural reading of the word's letters.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 21:17"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יכיר", :translit "yakir", :gloss "he recognizes"} {:he "לאחר", :translit "l'acher", :gloss "to another"} {:he "יכירנו לאחרים", :translit "yakhirnu l'acherim", :gloss "he recognizes him to others"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "יכיר", :b "לאחר"}], :frame {:text "The Sifrei on Deuteronomy 21:17 expounds the word יכיר — 'he recognizes' — to mean the father recognizes the firstborn to others, i.e., publicly acknowledges him. Ba'al HaTurim connects this derashah to a gematria equivalence between יכיר and לאחר.", :sources ["Sifrei Deuteronomy 215"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בכל", :translit "b'khol", :gloss "in all"} {:he "אשר ימצא לו", :translit "asher yimatze lo", :gloss "that is found to him"} {:he "כי", :translit "ki", :gloss "for"} {:he "ראוי", :translit "ra'uy", :gloss "fitting / worthy"} {:he "לא", :translit "lo", :gloss "no / not"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "בכל אשר ימצא לו כי", :spells "ראוי"} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "בכול ואל״ף דאשר", :spells "לא"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'בכל אשר ימצא לו' in Deuteronomy 21:17 limits the firstborn's double portion to property that the father actually possessed, excluding certain categories. The Gemara in Bavli Bekhorot 51b and Yerushalmi Bikkurim 3:3 discusses what the firstborn does and does not receive as a double portion, addressing items that are not fully 'fitting' for inclusion.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 21:17" "Bekhorot 51b" "Yerushalmi Bikkurim 3:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ראשית אונו", :translit "reshit ono", :gloss "first of his strength"} {:he "ראשית", :translit "reshit", :gloss "beginning / first"} {:he "ראשית דגנך", :translit "reshit daganekha", :gloss "first of your grain"} {:he "קדש ישראל לה'", :translit "kodesh yisra'el la'", :gloss "holiness of Israel to the Lord"} {:he "ראשית תבואתה", :translit "reshit t'vu'atah", :gloss "first of her produce"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Lexical pattern: every occurrence of the word ראשית carries the connotation of choice or selected portion"}], :frame {:text "The word ראשית denotes choicest or select portion across Scripture. The Midrash on Exodus 23:19 (ראשית ביכורי אדמתך) expounds ראשית as the best portion. Jeremiah 2:3 calls Israel קדש ישראל — the consecration/first of His produce. Proverbs 3:9 uses ראשית דגנך as the choice produce dedicated to God.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 21:17" "Exodus 23:19" "Jeremiah 2:3" "Proverbs 3:9"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לו משפט הבכרה", :translit "lo mishpat ha-b'khorah", :gloss "to him the right of the firstborn"}], :mechanisms [], :frame nil}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Orthographic observation: each letter of בכור exhibits doubling — bet doubled over preceding letter, kaf over preceding yod, resh likewise, and vav written as two vavs", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:a-value 240, :b-value 239, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "לאחר", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "יכיר"} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "בכל אשר ימצא לו כי", :spells "ראוי", :letters ["ב" "א" "י" "ל" "כ"], :by :selah, :order :mi